# Asymmetric clock: CLOCK clk 10 3 gives a 10-unit period that is LOW for
# 3 units, then HIGH for 7 (rising edges at 3, 13, 23, ...; falling at 10, 20, ...).
# See docs/formats/testbench.md#clock.
FSM tests/netlists/fsm/traffic_light/traffic_light_fsm.net
CLOCK clk 10 3
MAX_TIME 43

# Reset is asserted at t=0 and released before the first rising edge at t=3.
@0 reset=1 en=0
@1 reset=0 en=0

# Enable before subsequent rising edges at t=13, 23, and 33.
@8 en=1
ASSERT @14 G=0 Y=1 R=0 "First enabled rising edge advances Green to Yellow"
ASSERT @24 G=0 Y=0 R=1 "Second enabled rising edge advances Yellow to Red"
ASSERT @34 G=1 Y=0 R=0 "Third enabled rising edge advances Red to Green"
